      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301731",
      ":question/problem": "A town council wants to assess the opinions of all town residents about building a new community swimming pool.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Randomly selecting a sample of residents drawn from the town\u2019s swim-club membership list.\n2. Randomly selecting residents from a comprehensive town address registry (including renters and homeowners) and contacting them by phone or mail.\n3. Posting an online survey on the town website and inviting any resident to respond.\n4. Standing near the current public pool on a Saturday afternoon and randomly asking people for their opinions."
