      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-302204",
      ":question/problem": "A city council wants to assess the opinions of all city residents about building a new public dog park.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Standing near the current dog park on a Saturday afternoon and randomly asking people for their opinions.\n2. Posting an online survey on the city\u2019s website and inviting any resident to respond.\n3. Randomly selecting residents from a comprehensive city address registry (including renters and homeowners) and contacting them by phone or mail.\n4. Randomly selecting a sample of residents from the city\u2019s dog-owner registration list."
